// velt/crypto (tests): Ed25519 signing (`ed25519Sign`, `ed25519PublicKey`), run by
// `velt test std/`: RFC 8032 §7.1's first three tests, and keys and signatures made by another
// implementation (Python's `cryptography`, which signs with OpenSSL) for seeds of all zeros and
// all ones and for random seeds with messages around SHA-512's block and padding lengths; each
// signature also goes through `ed25519Verify`. The reduction mod L is checked on its own against
// Python's integers.
